nt><exTemp><TM_Instant><tmPosition>1994-07-23</tmPosition></TM_Instant></exTemp></TempExtent></tempEle></srcExt></dataSource><dataSource type=""><srcDesc>Geospatial data</srcDesc><srcMedName><MedNameCd value="015"/></srcMedName><srcCitatn><resTitle>Lake Urmia Iran</resTitle><resAltTitle>SouthWestern Bell WorldRoom</resAltTitle><citRespParty><rpOrgName>SouthWestern Bell WorldRoom</rpOrgName><role><RoleCd value="006"/></role></citRespParty><citRespParty><rpOrgName>SouthWestern Bell WorldRoom</rpOrgName><rpCntInfo><cntAddress><delPoint>online</delPoint></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="010"/></role></citRespParty><presForm><PresFormCd value="005"/></presForm><presForm><fgdcGeoform>remote-sensing image</fgdcGeoform></presForm><otherCitDet>Note: These photographs and the accompanying text are taken from the NASA Space Shuttle Earth Observations Photography Database.</otherCitDet><citOnlineRes><linkage>http://worldroom.tamu.edu/mideast/photos/41g-37-084.html</linkage></citOnlineRes></srcCitatn></dataSource><dataSource type=""><srcDesc>Geospatial data</srcDesc><srcMedName><MedNameCd value="015"/></srcMedName><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>http://landsat7.usgs.gov</resAltTitle><citRespParty><rpOrgName>U.S. Geological Society</rpOrgName><role><RoleCd value="006"/></role></citRespParty><citRespParty><rpOrgName>U.S. Geological Society</rpOrgName><rpCntInfo><cntAddress><delPoint>online</delPoint></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="010"/></role></citRespParty><presForm><PresFormCd value="005"/></presForm><presForm><fgdcGeoform>remote-sensing image</fgdcGeoform></presForm><datasetSeries><seriesName>Landsat PROGRAM</seriesName></datasetSeries><otherCitDet>This image appears to be no longer available.</otherCitDet><citOnlineRes><linkage>http://landsat7.usgs.gov/browse/titicaca.html</linkage></citOnlineRes></srcCitatn></dataSource><prcStep><stepDesc>The following steps were performed by Esri for Data &amp; Maps 2002: Downloaded Sea of Aral image from http://visibleearth.nasa.gov/data/ev89/ev8936_AralSea.A2001165.0710.250m.jpg. Locally registered the image to the vector data using ArcView® GIS Image Analysis creating shapefiles of the current water area. These shapefiles were used as the basis for updating the current extent of the rivers leading to the sea. Copied ArcGIS® layer file (.lyr), ArcView GIS legend file (.avl), and projection file (.prj) and created spatial indices. The following steps were performed by Esri: Extracted the features from ArcWorld 1:25M. Aligned the mouths of rivers with coastlines. Made features consistent with all political boundaries they are coincident with. Added attribute values from the Rand McNally New International Atlas, the Times Atlas of the World, the Digital Chart of the World, and World Resources Institute. Added St. Lawrence system from ArcWorld 1:3M. Generalized to match detail of the Cntry00.shp. Removed unneeded attributes. Created ArcGIS® layer file (.lyr). Created ArcView GIS legend file (.avl). Created projection file (.prj). Ran ArcView GIS Avenue™ request ExportClean, and created spatial indices.</stepDesc><stepDateTm>2002-01-30</stepDateTm><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>Times Atlas</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>Rand McNally Int.</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>NASA Visible Earth</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>DCW</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>ArcWorld 1:3M, ArcWorld 1:25M</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc></prcStep><prcStep><stepDesc>The following steps were performed by Esri: Downloaded all image sources from the online links. Locally registered the images to the vector data using ArcView GIS Image Analysis creating shapefiles of the current water areas. These shapefiles were used as the basis for updating the current extent of the rivers leading to these water areas. Created ArcGIS® layer file (.lyr), projection file (.prj), and spatial indices. Converted the data set to SDC.</stepDesc><stepDateTm>2002-09-25</stepDateTm><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>JSC DIC</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>http://landsat7.usgs.gov</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>SouthWestern Bell WorldRoom</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>NASA Visible Earth</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>Earthshots from the EROS</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc><stepSrc type="used"><srcCitatn><resAltTitle>NASA Earth Observatory</resAltTitle></srcCitatn></stepSrc></prcStep><prcStep><stepDesc>The following steps were performed by Esri: Added KILOMETERS attribute and calculated its values. Added MILES attribute and calculated its values.</stepDesc><stepDateTm>2004-03-07</stepDateTm></prcStep><prcStep><stepDesc>The following steps were performed by Esri: Deleted the shoreline (lake) features. The MILES and KILOMETERS attribute values were not recalculated. Reduced the attribute widths for NAME and SYSTEM. Corrected a spelling error.</stepDesc><stepDateTm>2005-02-15</stepDateTm></prcStep><prcStep><stepDesc>Converted the dataset into a file geodatabase.</stepDesc><stepDateTm>2014-04-01T00:00:00</stepDateTm></prcStep></dataLineage></dqInfo><mdHrLvName Sync="TRUE">dataset</mdHrLvName><refSysInfo><RefSystem><refSysID><identCode code="4326" Sync="TRUE"/><idCodeSpace Sync="TRUE">EPSG</idCodeSpace><idVersion Sync="TRUE">6.2(3.0.1)</idVersion></refSysID></RefSystem></refSysInfo><spatRepInfo><VectSpatRep><geometObjs Name="World_Major_Rivers"><geoObjTyp><GeoObjTypCd value="002" Sync="TRUE"></GeoObjTypCd></geoObjTyp><geoObjCnt Sync="TRUE">0</geoObjCnt></geometObjs><topLvl><TopoLevCd value="001" Sync="TRUE"></TopoLevCd></topLvl></VectSpatRep></spatRepInfo><mdDateSt Sync="TRUE">20251210</mdDat